course: dictionary
lesson: 15314
title: Slurred speech and slurred notes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to choose. «Her words were slurred after she woke up, so we could hardly understand her.» Here slurred means the words ran into each other and were hard to follow. The clue is hardly understand.
explain: Slurred is also a music word. «The violinist slurred the notes, so they flowed smoothly into one another.» A slur is a curved line over notes that tells you to play them smoothly, joined together. Look for clues like notes, music or a curved line.
explain: Slur can also mean an insult, but this meaning is less common. «He was hurt by the slur about his family.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Slurred means the sounds of words run into each other, so they are hard to understand.
fact: Slurred speech can be a warning sign of being very tired, ill or drunk.
fact: If someone's speech suddenly becomes slurred, with a drooping face or a weak arm, call the emergency number at once, as it may be a stroke.
fact: In music, «slurred» notes are played smoothly and joined together, shown by a curved line called a slur.
fact: A slur can also be an insult, so «slurred» can mean an unfair insult against someone.
exercise: «Her words were slurred after she woke up, so we could hardly understand her.» What does slurred mean here? | The words were written in gold ink | *The words ran into each other and were hard to understand | The words were sung loudly and clearly | The words were said on purpose in a whisper
exercise: In music class, the teacher says, «Play these notes slurred.» What does slurred mean? | Played with a short, sharp stop on each note | *Played smoothly, joined together | Played by someone else | Played as loudly as possible
exercise: Which is a warning sign that someone may need help quickly? | *Suddenly slurred speech with a drooping face and a weak arm | Speaking clearly while reading a book | A happy smile and a loud laugh | Singing a song at the party
test: «He was hurt by the slur, a cruel insult about his family.» What is a slur in this sentence? | A type of quiet speech | *An insult | A sunny day | A curved line in music
test: «The flute player slurred the high notes, so they sounded like one long, smooth sound.» What does slurred mean? | *Joined together smoothly | Whispered very softly | Played quickly and loudly | Missed out completely
exam: «After the long shift, Dad's voice was slurred and he kept yawning.» What does this suggest? | Dad has won a prize | Dad is singing a happy song | Dad is playing the violin | *Dad is very tired
